<article class="env-lemma" id="0BAR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BAR">Lemma <span data-tag="0BAR">66.11.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme and let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. The set of codimension $0$ points of $X$ is dense in $|X|$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      If $U$ is a scheme, then the set of generic points of irreducible components is dense in $U$ (holds for any quasi-sober topological space). Thus if $U \to X$ is a surjective étale morphism, then the set of codimension $0$ points of $X$ is the image of a dense subset of $|U|$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/0BAQ" data-tag="0BAQ">66.11.1</a>). Since $|X|$ has the quotient topology for $|U| \to |X|$ we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>